    "text": "**Case A**\n\n- **A1 \u2013 Cannot tell.** The search covered only the past seven days, and no coverage record is shown for that search. Misuse could have happened earlier, outside what was checked.\n- **A2 \u2013 Cannot tell.** No record shows what inputs the compromise check used when it scored at 30 minutes. We cannot say what evidence was available to it.\n- **A3 \u2013 No, not by itself.** A shared payout destination is a link between the accounts. It does not by itself prove they have one owner.\n- **A4 \u2013 No.** The only outcome channel shown is for monthly invoices, not for these payouts. If the payouts went to an attacker, the victim would be the account owner, who may never file a report. Silence here does not point to legitimacy.\n- **A5 \u2013 Yes.** The burst came from a new proxy and fingerprint just after publication. It changed the payout destination and sped up payouts. That clearly warrants investigation.\n\n**Case B**\n\n- **B1 \u2013 Cannot tell.** Chargebacks are \"recorded at\" each account. Only one link to a specific transaction is verified, and it is a refund at A, not a chargeback. We cannot confirm which account's transactions these chargebacks belong to.\n- **B2 \u2013 No.** The combined measure covers 400 transactions, so 5 percent is about 20 events. Those could be spread unevenly, leaving one account well above 5 percent.\n- **B3 \u2013 Cannot tell.** No coverage record is shown for the search for the controlling person. It is also unclear whether the search would catch other identities.\n- **B4 \u2013 Cannot tell.** The notes were written by different analysts on different days. They may still rest on the same evidence, and their sources are not shown.\n- **B5 \u2013 No.** A blocked payment never settled, so it could never get a chargeback. It should not be counted as a non-fraud transaction.\n- **B6 \u2013 Yes.** The shared templates, the shared descriptor pattern and the common settlement are enough to justify looking at the four accounts together.\n\nRESULT MO-043 | A1: Cannot tell | A2: Cannot tell | A3: No, not by itself | A4: No | A5: Yes | B1: Cannot tell | B2: No | B3: Cannot tell | B4: Cannot tell | B5: No | B6: Yes"
